      "title": "Three.js Part 8: Loading Models",
      "description": "An updated version of export/import workflows between Blender and three.js can be found here:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iPtlShz9i9A\n\nTHREE.js is an open source javascript library for 3D graphics on the web. In this lesson we discuss blender, a free 3D modeling tool, how to install a plugin for exporting content from blender to three.js. As well as, how to load models and animations exported from blender in three.js.\n\nNote: Due to browser security restrictions loading of files will not work on your local file system, so you will need to run the demos on a server for it to load the file.\n\nVersion 79 of THREE.js was used for the making of this video.  \n\nDownload the demo files here:\nhttps://github.com/diving-in/threejs/blob/master/threejs-7_models.zip\n\nMusic by: https://soundcloud.com/standingwave",
